            <ul>
              <li>Three companies and three years: this shows a method, not a market view.</li>
              <li>The DCF depends on assumptions that are illustrative. Terminal value is most of the result.</li>
              <li>The enterprise-to-equity bridge is partial (see above). Pharma litigation and contingent consideration can be material.</li>
              <li>No pipeline probability or patent-expiry modelling; a single revenue path per scenario.</li>
              <li>GSK: lease treatment inside borrowings is assumed, and non-controlling interests are understated at book value.</li>
              <li>No share-price data is bundled, so multiples need your own inputs.</li>
              <li>Not independently reviewed. Do not use it for investment decisions.</li>
